{"id":"code-count-inversions","title":"Count inversions efficiently","category":"code","difficulty":4,"prompt":"Write a Python function `count_inversions(values: list[int]) -> int` that returns the\nnumber of pairs (i, j) with i < j and values[i] > values[j]. The list can hold up to 50,000\nintegers and the function must finish in well under two seconds, so a quadratic scan is\ntoo slow. The input must not be modified.","system":"You are completing one task from an evaluation suite. Do the task as asked.\n\nReply with one Python code block that defines exactly what the task asks for. Use only the standard library. Do not include tests, examples, or print statements.","grader":{"type":"code","entrypoint":"count_inversions","tests":["assert count_inversions([]) == 0","assert count_inversions([1, 2, 3]) == 0","assert count_inversions([3, 2, 1]) == 3","assert count_inversions([2, 4, 1, 3, 5]) == 3","assert count_inversions([2, 2, 1]) == 2","assert count_inversions([1, 1, 1]) == 0","x = [3, 1, 2]; count_inversions(x); assert x == [3, 1, 2]","assert count_inversions(list(range(50000, 0, -1))) == 50000 * 49999 // 2","assert count_inversions([(i * 7919) % 50021 for i in range(50000)]) == 624860001"]},"reference":"```python\ndef count_inversions(values: list[int]) -> int:\n    def sort(items):\n        if len(items) <= 1:\n            return items, 0\n        mid = len(items) // 2\n        left, a = sort(items[:mid])\n        right, b = sort(items[mid:])\n        merged = []\n        count = a + b\n        i = j = 0\n        while i < len(left) and j < len(right):\n            if left[i] <= right[j]:\n                merged.append(left[i])\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                merged.append(right[j])\n                j += 1\n                count += len(left) - i\n        merged.extend(left[i:])\n        merged.extend(right[j:])\n        return merged, count\n\n    return sort(list(values))[1]\n```","answers":["```python\ndef count_inversions(values: list[int]) -> int:\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(len(values)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(values)):\n            if values[i] > values[j]:\n                count += 1\n    return count\n```","```python\ndef count_inversions(values: list[int]) -> int:\n    def sort(items):\n        if len(items) <= 1:\n            return items, 0\n        mid = len(items) // 2\n        left, a = sort(items[:mid])\n        right, b = sort(items[mid:])\n        merged = []\n        count = a + b\n        i = j = 0\n        while i < len(left) and j < len(right):\n            if left[i] <= right[j]:\n                merged.append(left[i])\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                merged.append(right[j])\n                j += 1\n                count += len(left) - i\n        merged.extend(left[i:])\n        merged.extend(right[j:])\n        return merged, count\n\n    return sort(list(values))[1]\n```"],"cells":[{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":0,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.77777778,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":7,"total":9,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"timeout"},{"ok":false,"error":"timeout"}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.024,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":168,"output_tokens":335,"cost_usd":0.0001843,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":1,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.77777778,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":7,"total":9,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"timeout"},{"ok":false,"error":"timeout"}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.024,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":168,"output_tokens":393,"cost_usd":0.0002133,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":2,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.77777778,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":7,"total":9,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":tr